{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nThe game of Egg Roulette is played between two players. Initially 2R raw eggs and 2C cooked eggs are placed randomly into a carton. The shells are left on so there is no way to distinguish a raw egg from a cooked egg. One at a time, a player will select an egg, and then smash the egg on his/her forehead. If the egg was cooked, not much happens, but if the egg was raw, it will make quite the mess. This continues until one player has broken R raw eggs, at which point that player is declared the loser and the other player wins.The order in which players take turns can be described as a string of 'A' and 'B' characters, where the i-th character tells which player should choose the i-th egg. Traditionally, players take turns going one after the other. That is, they follow the ordering \"ABABAB...\". This isn't very fair though, because the second player will win more often than the first. We'd like you to find a better ordering for the players to take their turns. Let's define the unfairness of an ordering as the absolute difference between the first player's win probability and the second player's win probability. We're interested in orderings that minimize the unfairness. We only consider an ordering valid if it contains the same number of 'A's as 'B's.You will also be given a string S of length 2(R\u2009+\u2009C) containing only 'A', 'B', and '?' characters. An ordering is said to match S if it only differs from S in positions where S contains a '?'. Of the valid orderings that minimize unfairness, how many match S?\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Test {\n    int readInt() {\n        int ans = 0;\n        boolean neg = false;\n        try {\n            boolean start = false;\n            for (int c = 0; (c = System.in.read()) != -1; ) {\n                if (c == '-') {\n                    start = true;\n                    neg = true;\n                    continue;\n                } else if (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n                    start = true;\n                    ans = ans * 10 + c - '0';\n                } else if (start) break;\n            }\n        } catch (IOException e) {\n        }\n        return neg ? -ans : ans;\n    }\n\n    int r, c;\n    Scanner sca = new Scanner(System.in);\n    long[][] C = new long[64][64];\n    long best = Long.MAX_VALUE;\n\n    void dfs(long x, long y, int v1, int v2) {\n        long d = Math.abs(x - y);\n        if (best <= 1 || d - C[v1][r]*C[v2][r] >= best) return;\n        if (v1 == r - 1 && v2 == r - 1) {\n            if (d < best) best = d;\n            return;\n        }\n        if (v1 >= r) {\n            long c1 = C[v1][r] - C[v1-1][r], s2 = C[v2][r];\n            dfs(x, y + c1*s2, v1 - 1, v2);\n        }\n        if (v2 >= r) {\n            long s1 = C[v1][r], c2 = C[v2][r] - C[v2-1][r];\n            dfs(x + s1*c2, y, v1, v2 - 1);\n        }\n    }\n\n    int[] cntA = new int[64], cntB = new int[64];\n    Map<Long, Long> cache = new TreeMap<>();\n    char[] cs;\n\n    long solve(long x, long y, int v1, int v2) {\n        long k = x*10000 + v1*100  + v2;\n        Long v = cache.get(k);\n        if (v != null) return v;\n        v = 0l;\n        long d = Math.abs(x - y);\n        if (d - C[v1][r]*C[v2][r] > best) {\n            cache.put(k, v);\n            return v;\n        }\n        if (v1 < r || v2 < r) {\n            int sum = v1 + v2;\n            if (v1 >= cntA[sum] && v2 >= cntB[sum]) {\n                v1 -= cntA[sum];\n                v2 -= cntB[sum];\n                v = C[v1+v2][v1];\n                cache.put(k, v);\n                return v;\n            }\n            cache.put(k, v);\n            return v;\n        }\n        char c = cs[v1 + v2 - 1];\n        if (c != 'B') {\n            long c1 = C[v1][r] - C[v1 - 1][r], s2 = C[v2][r];\n            v += solve(x, y + c1*s2, v1 - 1, v2);\n        }\n        if (c != 'A') {\n            long s1 = C[v1][r], c2 = C[v2][r] - C[v2-1][r];\n            v += solve( x + s1*c2, y, v1, v2 - 1);\n        }\n        cache.put(k, v);\n        return v;\n    }\n\n    void start() {\n        r = sca.nextInt(); c = sca.nextInt(); sca.nextLine();\n        cs = sca.nextLine().toCharArray();\n        for (int i = 0; i <= 2*(r + c); i++)\n            for (int j = 0; j <= 2*(r + c); j++) {\n                if (j == 0) C[i][j] = 1;\n                else if (i == 0) C[i][j] = 0;\n                else C[i][j] = C[i-1][j - 1] + C[i - 1][j];\n            }\n        int v1 = r + c, v2 = r + c;\n        long x = 0, y = 0;\n        while (v1 >= r && v2 >= 0) {\n            if (x > y) {\n                long c1 = C[v1][r] - C[v1 - 1][r], s2 = C[v2][r];\n                y += c1*s2;\n                v1--;\n            } else {\n                long s1 = C[v1][r], c2 = C[v2][r] - C[v2-1][r];\n                x += s1*c2;\n                v2--;\n            }\n        }\n        best = Math.abs(x - y);\n        dfs(0, 0, r + c, r + c);\n        for (int i = 0; i < 2*(r+c); i++) {\n            cntA[i + 1] = cntA[i] + (cs[i] == 'A' ? 1 : 0);\n            cntB[i + 1] = cntB[i] + (cs[i] == 'B' ? 1 : 0);\n        }\n        long ans = solve(0, 0, r + c, r + c);\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n\n        new Test().start();\n\n    }\n}\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    int r, c;\n    long[][] C = new long[64][64];\n    long bestUnfairness = Long.MAX_VALUE;\n    char[] pattern;\n    int[] cntA = new int[64];\n    int[] cntB = new int[64];\n    Map<Long, Long> memo = new HashMap<>();\n\n    long solve(long winsA, long winsB, int eggsA, int eggsB) {\n        if (eggsA < 0 || eggsB < 0) return 0;\n        \n        long key = (winsA << 20) ^ (winsB << 10) ^ (eggsA << 5) ^ eggsB;\n        if (memo.containsKey(key)) {\n            return memo.get(key);\n        }\n        \n        long total = 0;\n        int totalEggs = (r + c) * 2;\n        int used = (r + c) * 2 - eggsA - eggsB;\n        \n        if (eggsA == 0 && eggsB == 0) {\n            long unfairness = Math.abs(winsA - winsB);\n            if (unfairness < bestUnfairness) {\n                bestUnfairness = unfairness;\n                total = 1;\n            } else if (unfairness == bestUnfairness) {\n                total = 1;\n            }\n        } else {\n            if (used < totalEggs) {\n                char ch = pattern[used];\n                boolean canChooseA = (ch == 'A' || ch == '?');\n                boolean canChooseB = (ch == 'B' || ch == '?');\n                \n                if (canChooseA && eggsA > 0) {\n                    long c1 = C[eggsA - 1][r];\n                    long s2 = (eggsB > 0) ? C[eggsB - 1][r] : 0;\n                    total += solve(winsA + c1 * s2, winsB, eggsA - 1, eggsB);\n                }\n                \n                if (canChooseB && eggsB > 0) {\n                    long s1 = (eggsA > 0) ? C[eggsA - 1][r] : 0;\n                    long c2 = C[eggsB - 1][r];\n                    total += solve(winsA, winsB + s1 * c2, eggsA, eggsB - 1);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        memo.put(key, total);\n        return total;\n    }\n\n    void preprocess() {\n        for (int i = 0; i < 64; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {\n                if (j == 0 || j == i) {\n                    C[i][j] = 1;\n                } else {\n                    C[i][j] = C[i-1][j-1] + C[i-1][j];\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    void start() throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] firstLine = br.readLine().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        r = Integer.parseInt(firstLine[0]);\n        c = Integer.parseInt(firstLine[1]);\n        pattern = br.readLine().toCharArray();\n        \n        preprocess();\n        \n        int totalEggs = 2 * (r + c);\n        for (int i = 0; i < totalEggs; i++) {\n            cntA[i + 1] = cntA[i] + (pattern[i] == 'A' ? 1 : 0);\n            cntB[i + 1] = cntB[i] + (pattern[i] == 'B' ? 1 : 0);\n        }\n        \n        bestUnfairness = Long.MAX_VALUE;\n        memo.clear();\n        long result = solve(0, 0, r + c, r + c);\n        System.out.println(result);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        new Main().start();\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.344646857949556e-07, -2.682172998902388e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -8.129743218887597e-05, -8.821448318485636e-06, -0.016036108136177063, -0.28797727823257446, -1.6212332411669195e-05, -6.794906312279636e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00030393750057555735, -3.576272320060525e-06, -9.775113539944869e-06, -0.7569372653961182, -0.009764526039361954, -1